# Approved upstream bringup SHA256 allowlist (repository-controlled).
#
# Production Download and Prepare verifies the ACPS .sha1 sidecar, then requires
# SHA256(upstream bytes) to match one of these digests before the deterministic
# patcher may produce root-executable bringup output.
#
# HTTPS, same-channel SHA1 sidecars, and patch-anchor compatibility are NOT an
# approval root. New vendor bringup bytes must be reviewed and intentionally
# added here after patch compatibility/tests pass.
#
# Operational update process:
#   vendor releases new bringup
#     → acquisition detects unknown SHA256
#     → Download and Prepare fails closed (UPSTREAM_BRINGUP_PROVENANCE=FAIL)
#     → engineer reviews new upstream
#     → patch compatibility/tests run
#     → approved SHA256 is intentionally added below
#     → normal preparation can proceed
#
# Format: <sha256>  <label>

# Synthetic regression fixture (tests/fixtures/dp-phase2/upstream_bringup_unpatched.sh)
f912e81632fce481a0ce9b597779b14dbab45873321d137adc09c5e40adfffe5  upstream_bringup_unpatched

